\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Real hopping across a link}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Let a finite group act by isometries of a real inner product space.
Use the [orbit gauge–Higgs weight](fdip-010A) with site factors one
and edge functions #{b_e(u,v)=\ue^{w_e\langle u,v\rangle}} for real
#{w_e}. The product of its edge factors is
##{\prod_{e\in E}\ue^{w_e\langle\phi_{h(e)},U_e\phi_{s(e)}\rangle}.}
Taking all links equal to the identity recovers the [global hopping
weight](fdip-00ZW). For signs the inner product in the exponent is
#{\phi_{h(e)}U_e\phi_{s(e)}}. If #{w_e>0}, transported agreement
has weight #{\ue^{w_e}} and transported disagreement has weight
#{\ue^{-w_e}}. On a square complex the [Wilson action](fdip-006O)
gives one choice of face factors through its real exponential
#{\ue^{-S_W(U)}}.}
